:0.02975735172943675,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":44.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.008007061385670866,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":60.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010070472658288143,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":83.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.04753,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":31.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.111,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":11.1,"pf":[],"description_full":"Hamilton Insurance Group, Ltd., through its subsidiaries, operates as specialty insurance and reinsurance company in Bermuda and internationally. It operates Hamilton Global Specialty, Hamilton Select, and Hamilton Re underwriting platforms. The company offers casualty reinsurance products, such as commercial auto, general liability, healthcare, multiline, personal motor, professional liability, umbrella and excess casualty, and worker's compensation and employer's liability reinsurance; property reinsurance and insurance; and specialty reinsurance solutions, including accident and health, aviation and space, crisis management, mortgage, financial risks, marine and energy, and multiline specialty. It also provides accident and health, cyber, energy, environmental, financial lines, fine art and specie, kidnap and ransom, mergers and acquisitions, marine and energy liability, political risk and violence, professional liability, property binders, property direct and facultative, professional lines, space, upstream energy, excess casualty, war and terrorism, allied medical, products liability and contractors, management liability, medical professionals, general liability, and small business casualty insurance plans, as well as surety and treaty reinsurance products. The company was incorporated in 2013 and is headquartered in Pembroke, Bermuda.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Giuseppina Carmela Albo | CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $5.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 600 people. Revenue per employee of $4.8M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 36%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $49K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Hamilton Insurance Group, Ltd. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.8B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +36% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 44% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 37-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 42\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6052631578947361},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (89% sell ratio, net $6.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 87% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Valued at a 75% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"HG (OTCMKTS:STLY) Posts Quarterly Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/hg-otcmktsstly-posts-quarterly-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794583615.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Hamilton Insurance Group (HG) Undervalued On Earnings Upgrades And A Higher Analyst Rating?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-hg/hamilton-insurance-group/news/is-hamilton-insurance-group-hg-undervalued-on-earnings-upgra","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579676.322,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","analyst_action"]},{"title":"Hamilton Insurance Group (NYSE:HG) Sets New 52-Week High \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/hamilton-insurance-group-nysehg-sets-new-52-week-high-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794497730.0,"orig